{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["occ"],"tokens":[{"text":"@interface","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer","text":"MLNVectorStyleLayer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)MLNVectorStyleLayer"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A heatmap visualizes the spatial distribution of a large, dense set of point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data, using color to avoid cluttering the map with individual points at low"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zoom levels. The points are weighted by an attribute you specify. Use a heatmap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"style layer in conjunction with point or point collection features. These"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"features can come from vector tiles loaded by an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object, or they can be "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{